# Web frontend

- `src/core/` is pure TypeScript. It must not import React or three.js.
- The plan view is SVG in React (`src/editor/PlanSvg.tsx`), drawn from `src/drawing/scene.ts`, the same items the sheet compiler uses. Each element is its own hit shape. Tools call core operations. Tools are state machines, not boolean piles on the stage.
- Plan Y is up. Convert to screen Y in one view module.
- Picking uses `rbush`. Undo uses `immer` patches. Wall polygons use `polygon-clipping`.
- Autosave on pointer-up or a short debounce, never on every pointer-move. Send the revision. A 409 reloads the plan and shows an error.
- PDF and SVG come from `src/drawing/` draw commands, not from a screenshot of the view.

```typescript
// Bad: core importing the view
import PlanSvg from "@/editor/PlanSvg.tsx";

// Good: core returns points, the view maps them
const poly = wallPolygon(wall, joins);
```
